        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Step by Step guide: Build a Voice Agent That Never Goes Silent using ADK]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[The open-source Agent Development Kit (ADK) and gemini-3.8-live enable developers to build responsive voice agents by implementing non-blocking tools in Python. Developers can use streaming tools to yield progress updates or background execution patterns to keep conversations fluid during long-running backend queries. Additionally, configuring response scheduling behaviors such as WHEN_IDLE, INTERRUPT, or SILENT gives developers precise control over when and how tool results are delivered into the conversation.]]></description>
            <link>https://developers.googleblog.com/step-by-step-guide-build-a-voice-agent-that-never-goes-silent-using-adk/</link>
            <guid isPermaLink="false">https://developers.googleblog.com/step-by-step-guide-build-a-voice-agent-that-never-goes-silent-using-adk/</guid>
            <pubDate>Thu, 12 Mar 2020 00:24:00 GMT</pubDate>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Three layers, one repo: a tour of google/adk-recipes]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[The google/adk-recipes repository unifies Agent Development Kit (ADK) resources into three structured layers—core/, plugins/, and contrib/—serving as a single source of truth for building AI agents. Developers can leverage reference patterns, install modular vertical skills (such as retail product search and virtual try-on) directly into their coding assistants, and deploy production-ready services across multiple languages. This cohesive structure streamlines the entire workflow from initial scaffolding to full deployment on Google Cloud infrastructure.]]></description>
            <link>https://developers.googleblog.com/three-layers-one-repo-a-tour-of-googleadk-recipes/</link>
            <guid isPermaLink="false">https://developers.googleblog.com/three-layers-one-repo-a-tour-of-googleadk-recipes/</guid>
            <pubDate>Sun, 01 Mar 2020 07:20:00 GMT</pubDate>
        </item>
