        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Announcing DPoP Support for Google OAuth: Securing Refresh Tokens]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[Google OAuth Platform now supports DPoP (Demonstrating Proof-of-Possession) to sender-constrain refresh tokens, neutralizing Infostealer malware and adversary-in-the-middle attacks. By cryptographically binding long-lived refresh tokens while maintaining short-lived access tokens as standard Bearer tokens, developers achieve robust credential security without incurring high-QPS API performance overhead. Additionally, developers integrating multi-agent or Model Context Protocol (MCP) workloads can use Google Cloud Secure Token Service (STS) to handle secure token delegation across agent chains.]]></description>
            <link>https://developers.googleblog.com/announcing-dpop-support-for-google-oauth-securing-refresh-tokens/</link>
            <guid isPermaLink="false">https://developers.googleblog.com/announcing-dpop-support-for-google-oauth-securing-refresh-tokens/</guid>
            <pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2020 09:22:00 GMT</pubDate>
        </item>
